  "lineage": "Low-pitched bagpipe tradition of Bulgaria's Rhodope mountains, played on the kaba gaida whose chanter sounds roughly a fourth below the northern djura gaida, documented from the early twentieth century and institutionalised through the Shiroka Laka music school and the 100 Kaba Gaidi mass ensemble founded in 1961, characterised by slow rubato bavna pesen accompaniment, dense flick-ornament kavals of grace notes, a continuous low drone and slow Rhodope horo in 2/4 or 7/8 under wide open-throat female singing.",
